 # Fractal Brownian Motion
 
-Also called: Fractional Brownian Motion, Octave Perlin Noise, 3D Perlin Noise with Fractal Brownian Motion (FBM), 3D Perlin-like Noise, 3D Perlin-like Noise and Fractal Brownian Motion (FBM)
+Also called: 3D Perlin Noise with Fractal Brownian Motion (FBM), 3D Perlin-like Noise, 3D Perlin-like Noise and Fractal Brownian Motion (FBM), Fractional Brownian Motion, Octave Perlin Noise
 
 ## Overview
-Fractal Brownian Motion (FBM) is a procedural noise construction that generates self-similar, multi-scale stochastic patterns by summing multiple octaves of a base noise function with increasing frequency and decreasing amplitude [S4][S7, S9, unofficial]. It solves the problem of creating natural-looking textures (such as clouds, terrain, or marble) that lack the repetitive, low-frequency artifacts of single-octave noise [S4]. Unlike its sibling [Simplex Noise](978-simplex-noise.md) or [Value Noise](4008-value-noise.md), which define the local interpolation behavior, FBM defines the spectral summation strategy across scales [22470-tileable-noise-generation.md].
+Fractal Brownian Motion (FBM) is a procedural noise construction that generates self-similar, multi-scale stochastic patterns by summing multiple octaves of a base noise function with increasing frequency and decreasing amplitude [S4][S7, S9, unofficial]. It solves the problem of creating fractal-like noise with many frequencies by combining variations of a single base noise function whose parameters are scaled differently [S4]. Unlike its sibling [Simplex Noise](978-simplex-noise.md) or [Value Noise](4008-value-noise.md), which define the local interpolation behavior, FBM defines the spectral summation strategy across scales [22470-tileable-noise-generation.md].
 
 ## How it works
-FBM constructs a fractal noise field by evaluating a base gradient noise function (such as [Perlin Noise](3860-gradient-based-noise-perlin-simplex.md)) at multiple scales and summing the results. The base noise provides smooth, continuous values, while the summation introduces high-frequency detail.
